        "original_id": "b5d9a61e-b523-584b-898b-02036d8e965d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Rufus Sewell, Jude Law, Jack Black, Eli Wallach, Shannyn Sossamon, Edward Burns, Kenneth Branagh\n- Works: The Holiday, Hamlet, The Woodlanders, Dangerous Beauty, Dark City, A Knight's Tale, The Illusionist, Tristan and Isolde, Martha, Meet Frank, Daniel and Laurence\n- Roles: Graham, Miles, Fortinbras\n\nFacts:\n- Rufus Frederik Sewell was born on 29 October 1967 and is an English actor.\n- In 1996, Rufus Sewell appeared in Kenneth Branagh's film rendition of Hamlet and played Fortinbras.\n- Rufus Sewell has also appeared in the films The Woodlanders, Dangerous Beauty, Dark City, A Knight's Tale, The Illusionist, Tristan and Isolde, and Martha, Meet Frank, Daniel and Laurence.\n- In The Holiday, Jude Law and Jack Black were cast as the leading men Graham and Miles.\n- In The Holiday, Eli Wallach, Shannyn Sossamon, Edward Burns, and Rufus Sewell played key supporting roles.",
